.\" fbsd-config.7 - overview of FreeBSD system configuration
.\" Written in mdoc(7). Render with: mandoc -T utf8 fbsd-config.7
.Dd October 15, 2026
.Dt FBSD-CONFIG 7
.Os FreeBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm fbsd-config
.Nd overview of FreeBSD system configuration files
.Sh DESCRIPTION
FreeBSD keeps its system configuration in a small number of plain text files,
mostly under
.Pa /etc
and
.Pa /boot .
This page is a quick map of where each kind of setting lives and
which tool to use to change it.
.Pp
Settings fall into three layers:
.Bl -enum -offset indent
.It
Boot-time kernel and module settings, read by the loader.
.It
Runtime kernel settings, applied with
.Xr sysctl 8 .
.It
Userland services and networking, started by
.Xr rc 8 .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /boot/loader.conf" -compact
.It Pa /etc/rc.conf
Main system configuration: hostname, network interfaces, services to enable.
Site overrides go here; defaults live in
.Pa /etc/defaults/rc.conf
and should not be edited.
.It Pa /etc/rc.conf.d/
Optional per-service fragments, one file per service.
.It Pa /boot/loader.conf
Boot loader variables and kernel modules to load at boot.
.It Pa /etc/sysctl.conf
Kernel state variables applied at boot time.
.It Pa /etc/fstab
File systems and swap to mount at boot.
.It Pa /etc/resolv.conf
DNS resolver settings.
.It Pa /etc/ssh/sshd_config
Configuration for the OpenSSH server.
.It Pa /etc/pf.conf
Rules for the
.Xr pf 4
packet filter.
.It Pa /etc/make.conf
Build options used when compiling ports and the base system.
.It Pa /etc/periodic.conf
Settings for the daily, weekly and monthly
.Xr periodic 8
jobs.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Enable the SSH daemon and set a hostname using
.Xr sysrc 8 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# sysrc sshd_enable=YES
# sysrc hostname="myhost.example.org"
.Ed
.Pp
A minimal
.Pa /etc/rc.conf :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
hostname="myhost.example.org"
ifconfig_em0="DHCP"
sshd_enable="YES"
ntpd_enable="YES"
.Ed
.Pp
Load a module at boot in
.Pa /boot/loader.conf :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
zfs_load="YES"
kern.vty="vt"
.Ed
.Pp
Start, stop or restart a service after changing its settings:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# service sshd restart
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr loader.conf 5 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr sysctl.conf 5 ,
.Xr fstab 5 ,
.Xr pf.conf 5 ,
.Xr sysrc 8 ,
.Xr service 8 ,
.Xr sysctl 8 ,
.Xr rc 8
.Sh AUTHORS
